<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Mortgage Guide (Investment).</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Mortgage Guide (Investment).</headline>
<text>
<p>(Updated on December 27)</p>
<p>LENDER	 VARIABLE   INTRO RATES *TRUE RATE</p>
<p>Adelaide	 8.25	    6.40	 8.05</p>
<p>Advance	  8.25	    7.75	 8.33</p>
<p>AIDC	     7.70	     -	   7.83</p>
<p>AMPs Priority  7.47	     -	   7.58</p>
<p>ANZ		8.25	    7.50	 8.23</p>
<p>Aussie Home    7.49	     -	   7.60</p>
<p>Austral	  7.35	     -	   7.46</p>
<p>BNZ		7.39	     -	   7.39</p>
<p>Bank of Melb   8.75	    6.95	 8.52</p>
<p>Bank SA	  8.25	     -	   8.29</p>
<p>BankWest	 8.25	    6.95	 8.18</p>
<p>BMC Mortgage   7.25	     -	   7.39</p>
<p>CHS HomeLoans  7.40	     -	   7.50</p>
<p>*The true rate takes into account fees and the introductory rate based on a typical A$100,000 loan, using total monthly payments over seven years which is the average life of a mortgage. The interest rate used after the initial fixed/capped period is a variable rate.</p>
<p>Source: Cannex</p>
<p>-- Reuters Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
